**Theorem 17.3 (earned exponent and exact unknown-gap acquisition).**
For every $h\in\mathcal H_A$ and every legal nuisance sequence,
Construction 17.2 terminates. With $R=Q(h)+1$ used only as proof
notation, its acquired certificate satisfies

$$
R<L,\qquad p_*<2(3R+1),\qquad d=1+\log_2p_*.
\tag{17.3}
$$

The extracted block, recovered historical field and actual returned
field are

$$
Y=OTx_h,\qquad
x_h=T^{-1}DY,\qquad
v=T^{n+1}x_h.
\tag{17.4}
$$

Thus Theorem 4.1 recovers the unique entire $h$. The current predictor
and autonomous block $m=Ov$ can be retained under the actual callable
context. No bound for $Q$ is supplied, and no physical inverse occurs.

Proof. Observation 3.3 shows that immediately before each historical
birth the old field is positive; a final raw birth can leave only its
fresh cells zero. Each such cell has a positive old neighbor. Therefore
$z=Tx_h$ is positive everywhere, also for alpha. Induction over the
actual historical and scout Ticks, using their integer numerator
matrix $4\operatorname{Id}+A$, gives

$$
z_a\in8^{-R}\mathbb Z,\qquad
z_a\ge8^{-R},\qquad
0<z_a\le\|z\|_\infty\le\lambda^R
\quad(a\in V_t).
\tag{17.5}
$$

Zero extensions preserve the common denominator and do not increase
the sup norm. These are the arithmetic inductions of Proposition 13.4
with the present actual Tick count, not a known-$Q$ input.

At any scout precision $p\ge3R+1$, the scaled terminal is at least
two. Its lower report is therefore at least two, so every allowed
report passes. The first power of two at least $3R+1$ is strictly
smaller than $2(3R+1)$; hence the stopping rule and bounds for $p_*,d$
hold on every nuisance path. At the successful Read the actual law gives

$$
2^{-p_*}\le(k_*-1)2^{-p_*}\le z_{\ell_1}\le\lambda^R.
\tag{17.6}
$$

Indeed $\lfloor2^{p_*}z_{\ell_1}\rfloor\ge k_*-1$.
Since $2\cdot7^6=235298<262144=8^6$, one has
$\lambda^6<1/2$. Consequently
$\lambda^{6p_*}<2^{-p_*}\le\lambda^R$, forcing $R<6p_*=L$.
This finite integer calculation earns the certificate from that actual
report. Neither an unknown exponent nor an exact-real logarithm is read.

At assay epoch $r$, the actual field is $T^rz$. Its denominator divides
$8^{R+r}$, which divides $2^M$ because $R+r<L+n$.
Write its terminal value as $a_{r,j}/2^M$ with an integer
$a_{r,j}\ge0$. The actual report is
$k_{r,j}=2a_{r,j}+\zeta_{r,j}$. Formula (17.2) extracts that same
$a_{r,j}/2^M$ for either bit. This is pointwise exact, with no averaging,
independence or repeated-noise assumption. The executed epochs therefore
give $Y=Oz$. The earned-tree forcing identity $DO=\operatorname{Id}$
gives (17.4). Theorem 4.1 applies to the original known-unit,
separated raw history after the one local inverse $T^{-1}$; its
hypotheses have not changed. The $n+1$ real acquisition Ticks give $v$.
The local current prediction $m=Ov$ introduces no further source Tick.
Every loop is finite on this promised domain. $\square$

